+#pragma mark -
+#pragma mark MVKMetalBinaryArchives
+
+/**
+ * RewindBox prototype (lot 7): Metal binary archives of the pipelines a device creates, kept on disk between sessions.
+ *
+ * Disabled unless the environment variable RBX_MVK_BINARY_ARCHIVE_DIR names a directory when the VkDevice is created:
+ * MVKDevice::getMetalBinaryArchives() then returns null and every pipeline is created exactly as upstream.
+ *
+ * Lookup: before a render or compute pipeline is compiled (MVKRenderPipelineCompiler, MVKComputePipelineCompiler: every
+ * pipeline MoltenVK creates, with the very MTL descriptor it compiles; inside the compiler's own block, so under the
+ * same device lock and compile timeout), the archives loaded at device creation are
+ * offered through the descriptor's binaryArchives and the pipeline is requested with
+ * MTLPipelineOptionFailOnBinaryArchiveMiss: Metal either returns the pipeline from an archive (a proven reuse) or fails
+ * at once (a miss), and the normal compilation then runs unchanged. With RBX_MVK_BINARY_ARCHIVE_STRICT=1 (tests only) a
+ * miss fails the pipeline instead.
+ *
+ * Collection: a pipeline that was compiled normally has a copy of its descriptor queued on one utility-priority serial
+ * queue, where its functions are added to this session's archive (Metal reuses the binary it just compiled). The
+ * creating thread never waits for it. A pipeline compiled while the archives were still loading is first looked up
+ * there, on the queue, so that nothing is added twice. After each save the session's archive is reopened from its
+ * file, so the binaries collected so far are no longer held in memory. The session's archive is written when 64 pipelines were added, when the
+ * application reads its Vulkan pipeline cache data (its own persistence points), and when the device is destroyed.
+ *
+ * Files: <directory>/id-<identity>/seg-<number>-<session token>-<bytes>-<sha256 prefix>.mtlarchive. The identity covers what makes Metal
+ * binaries unusable (this schema, the Vulkan pipelineCacheUUID: MoltenVK revision, OS version, GPU family, argument
+ * buffers; the OS build; the GPU name). Each session writes its own segment: a temporary file, then one rename to a name
+ * that carries its size and checksum, then the removal of the segment's previous generation. Earlier segments are never
+ * rewritten. At load a segment whose size or checksum does not match its name is removed; one Metal refuses is kept
+ * once and removed at its second refusal; the oldest segments beyond the count or size bounds are removed.
+ *
+ * A failure here never fails a pipeline (outside the strict test mode) and touches no other cache.
+ */
+class MVKMetalBinaryArchives : public MVKBaseDeviceObject {
+
+public:
+
+	/** Returns the Vulkan API opaque object controlling this object. */
